title: 'M1.12 slice 3 reading: what gnomon replay folds (G-KRN-01)'
summary: 'Replay runs verifyLog, then a deterministic fold of the envelope bytes into gnomon-replay:v1: per-session kernel-controlled inputs, recorded host-layer hashes, card states, head and kind counts. projectionHash is sha256 over canonicalJson. A divergence is a turn.sent whose contentHash is not the session''s last logged inject, or string inject bytes whose sha256 differs from the logged hash; it is refused INTEGRITY_BROKEN.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#kernel-log'
files_created:
  - packages/gnomon/src/kernel/log/replay.ts
  - packages/gnomon/src/cli/replay-cli.ts
  - packages/gnomon/test/m112-replay.test.ts
learnings:
  - The kernel has no projection tables yet
  - so the spec's projection hash had to be defined here
  - 'Replay stays inside #kernel-log (verify plus a fold over the same chain) and adds no Appendix A node'
  - Offline verify reads only keys/kernel-pub.jsonl; rows signed by registry keys fail there (residual)
body: 'Spec §2.1 and §3.3 scope G-KRN-01 to kernel-controlled inputs plus recorded host hashes, not host context. The fold carries: inputs (session.inject, turn.sent); host (the *Hash fields of session.spawned and session.layers.changed, recorded and never reproduced); cards (last state); head; kinds. No clock or environment input enters the fold. An unverified log is never folded. Observed while reading: supervisor.ts:560 and local-session.ts:441 log session.inject with bytes set to the text, but checkPayload (kernel-log.ts:2105) requires an integer, so a real daemon would refuse session.send. The fold accepts both forms and re-hashes string bytes. The bug itself is left for the #supervisor lane.'
